.TH ggh 1 "" "ggh 0.4.0-beta.3"
.SH NAME
ggh \- Git and GitHub in one CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ggh
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Git and GitHub in one CLI: pull requests, issues, CI, stacked branches, and AI. Anything \fBggh\fR does not recognise goes straight to \fBgit\fR, so \fBggh add .\fR, \fBggh push\fR, and \fBggh rebase \-i\fR behave exactly as \fBgit\fR does.
