.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every command follows the same rules.
.TP
\fB--json\fR
Machine-readable output on stdout, nothing else.
.TP
\fB--dry\-run\fR
Describe what would happen; change nothing.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB--yes\fR
Answer every confirmation with yes.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB--quiet\fR
Suppress progress; errors still print.
.TP
\fB--no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail with instructions instead.
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB--repo\fR \fIowner/name\fR
Act on another repository from anywhere (GitHub commands).
.RS
.PP
stdout is data. stderr is everything else. When \fBggh\fR needs an answer and there is no terminal, it cancels and exits non-zero rather than guessing.
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBGH_HOST\fR
Target a GitHub Enterprise host instead of github.com.
.TP
\fBGGH_*\fR
Per-key overrides (\fBGGH_AI_PROVIDER\fR, \fBGGH_CODEX_MODEL\fR, \fBGGH_AI_TIMEOUT_MS\fR, ...). Flags beat environment, environment beats config files.
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR, \fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR
Respected for config, plugins, aliases, and cache.
.TP
\fBGGH_DEBUG\fR
Print git-forwarding and alias-expansion decisions to stderr.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/good-gh/config.json\fR
User configuration (see \fBggh config\fR).
.TP
\fI~/.config/good-gh/aliases.json\fR, \fI~/.config/good-gh/plugins/\fR
Aliases and community plugins. Plugins run with full process privileges; install only from sources you trust.
.TP
\fI.ggh.json\fR (repository root)
Per-project configuration, safe to commit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Inspect a pull request as data:
ggh pr --json | jq -r '.[] | "\\(.number) \\(.title)"'
.TP
Commit with an AI message, then open a PR:
ggh commit --push --pr
.TP
Preview anything destructive first:
ggh discard --all --dry\-run
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, non-zero on failure. \fBggh\fR is usable as a gate in scripts and CI: failures set the exit code, and \fB--json\fR output stays parseable.
